%description:

Tcp.stopOperationExtraTime:other-segment -- a segment that reaches TCP in the extra time does not stop the run.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "Extra time after lifecycle stop operation finished".

The classes: zero (0s, the default: the stage of TCP ends at once, after the other events of
the same time) and other (a positive time: the stage ends the value later; the network layer
and the layers under it stay up until then). The code: OperationalMixin::
startActiveOperationExtraTimeOrFinish() schedules the end of the stage the value later, and
sets the state of TCP to down at once. The facet other-segment: in the extra time the network layer of host1 is up, so it gives
each arriving segment to TCP, which is down already. TCP takes no part: the segment gets no
answer, and the run goes on. This test separates "other" from "zero", where the network layer
is down and the segment does not reach TCP. This test fails: Tcp does not override
handleMessageWhenDown(), so OperationalMixin stops the run with "Message 'SYN' received when
Tcp is down" (finding PF-14).

Host under test: host1; host1 has no application. host2 sends a ping to host1 every 50 ms from 0.525 s on, so the
ping n leaves at 0.525 s + n * 50 ms. The tester stops host1 at 1.0 s with the lifecycle
operation of INET (stopNode). The stages of the stop go from the applications down: the
network layer of host1 goes down, and stops to answer pings, when the stage of TCP ends. In addition, host2 opens a TCP connection to host1 at 1.5 s.
Observation: level 1, the SYN of host2 leaves at 1.5 s, the last reply that host2 gets is the
reply to the ping 29 (1.975 s), and the run goes on to its end.

%# parameter: Tcp.stopOperationExtraTime
%# class: other-segment
%# value: 1s
%# key: *.host1.tcp.stopOperationExtraTime
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpStopOperationExtraTimeOtherSegment")
        .once(on("host2.app[0]").signal("pingRxSeq")
                  .filterValue(0)
                  .describe("the reply to the first ping")
                  .within(0.6))
        .act(action().at(1.0).stopNode("host1").describe("stop host1"))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.destPort == 1000")
             .describe("the SYN of host2, in the extra time of host1")
             .within(0.6))
        .once(on("host2.app[0]").signal("pingRxSeq")
                  .filterValue(29)
                  .describe("the reply to the ping 29, sent at 1.975 s")
                  .within(0.485))
        .never(on("host2.app[0]").signal("pingRxSeq")
                   .filterValueAtLeast(30)
                   .describe("a reply after the end of the stage of TCP")
                   .within(3.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpStopOperationExtraTimeOtherSegment compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.stopOperationExtraTime = 1s    # the parameter under test
*.host2.numApps = 2
*.host2.app[1].typename = "TcpSessionApp"
*.host2.app[1].connectAddress = "host1"
*.host2.app[1].connectPort = 1000
*.host2.app[1].tOpen = 1.5s
*.host2.app[1].tSend = 1.6s
*.host2.app[1].sendBytes = 1000B
*.host2.app[1].tClose = 1000s
*.host1.numApps = 0
*.host2.numApps = 1
*.host2.app[0].typename = "PingApp"
*.host2.app[0].destAddr = "host1"
*.host2.app[0].startTime = 0.525s
*.host2.app[0].sendInterval = 0.05s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpStopOperationExtraTimeOtherSegment: PASS
